# AWS credentials for `pnpm upload -- --execute` (uploads generated llms.txt
# files to S3). Copy this file to .env in this same directory and fill in
# real values - .env is gitignored, .env.sample is not.
#
# These are the same credentials/env var names used for S3 uploads elsewhere
# in the platform (platform/nextjs-extension/src/s3Connection/s3connector.ts,
# via platform/docs-nextjs/.env) - reuse those values here rather than
# creating new ones.
#
# AWS_SESSION_TOKEN is only needed for temporary/federated credentials (e.g.
# AWS SSO instead of a permanent IAM user access key). If you copied these
# from `aws sts get-session-token` or an SSO login, you need this too -
# leave it blank for a permanent IAM access key. The most common cause of
# "The AWS Access Key Id you provided does not exist in our records" is a
# temporary key pasted without its matching session token.

# To find these values, go to okta, AWS, docs platform, access keys
AWS_S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
AWS_S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
AWS_SESSION_TOKEN=
